   368	## 6. FALLACY-v2 audit
   369	
   370	- **Raw remainder degree.** Declared throughout: `6264` is the first of 118 constant
   371	  residues (and their gcd) in the charged integral basis; `64` is a normal form after 66
   372	  pivots. Neither is presented as an invariant. `reduce`/`std` were run in the declared
   373	  ring with `option(redSB)`; zero cases were handled explicitly (`[x^7 y^14] J = 0` is
   374	  reported as a vanished row, not as an absent one).
   375	- **Variable/ring map.** The map `B1c_{r,q} <-> x^{K-1-r-q}(y-x)^q`, `row (D,k) <->
   376	  [x^{D-k}y^k] J`, generator order and coefficient field `Q` are declared in §2.1 and
   377	  validated numerically against the frozen ledger by two independent routes. Matching
   378	  names were not used as evidence.
   379	- **Floor / attainment.** The `k0` value `e*A*(K-p)` is **derived**; the `k > k0` ladder
   380	  is a 66/66 **fit** and is labelled as such. It is a description of the reduced rows,
   381	  not a theorem about the unreduced system.
   382	- **Carrier / attainment.** `(16,12)` `dim = -1` is emptiness of the declared localised
   383	  chart, not a statement about any polynomial pair; no `REPRESENTATIVE` or
   384	  `FULL_ACTUAL_EXIT` claim is made anywhere.
   385	- **`sat()` wrapping.** Not used. Localisation is by Rabinowitsch variable only
   386	  (`Z*cst-1`), with positive and negative controls run in the same ring: raw `dim = 10`,
   387	  empty control `-1`, point control `0`, `reduce(1,GB) = 0`.
   388	- **Flag / place / series.** The three kill orders `0, 0, 1` (and `2` at `(16,12)`) are
   389	  reported per (chart, declared open condition). They are **not** identified as one
   390	  invariant, and the four charts are not claimed to be instances of one filtration.
   391	- **Prime label / derivative.** `p'`-type marks are avoided; `p_red` denotes the
   392	  squarefree part, stated explicitly, not a derivative.
   393	- **Fit vs proof.** The headline negative (§4) rests on a search over two bounded
   394	  grammars plus a structural argument (non-invariance over `Q`). The search alone would
