   140	## Source Audit: Common `h3`
   141	
   142	Moh Definition 5.1 defines one tower of major discs, with one general point in
   143	each disc, carrying simultaneous root counts for `g` and the approximate-root
   144	family; see the extracted source at
   145	`box/g108gate-20260903/moh_p179_196.txt:65` and `:89`.  The tower is common,
   146	not one tower per final child.
   147	
   148	Xu §7.3 supplies the principal-minor leading data.  It introduces
   149	quasi-approximate roots `T_i` for the pair at
   150	`box/g108gate-20260903/xu_p10_13.txt:21`, states the principal-minor
   151	multiplicities at `:25`, and writes the leading coefficients in terms of a
   152	single polynomial `p(pi)` at `:47` with `deg p=u_s` at `:51`.  In the split
   153	case, Corollary 7.5 explicitly writes one product
   154	`p(pi)=(pi-c1)...(pi-c_us)` with distinct roots at `:112`-`:119`, and the same
   155	single `p` is used in the leading forms of `f`, `g`, and `(T_s)_f` at
   156	`:115`-`:127`.
   157	
   158	Therefore the two 12-packets at `delta=3` are roots of one quadratic `p`; they
   159	share the same pre-extension `h3` leading polynomial.  At the child step
   160	`delta'=4`, each packet may have its own final local continuation, but that is
   161	after restricting to one root of the same `p`.  Replacing this by two unrelated
   162	`h3` polynomials is not a sourced weakening; it changes the Moh/Xu tower.
   163	
   164	What is conventional:
   165	
   166	* The translation gauge `p=pi^2-c` is a chart normalization.  Weakening it to
   167	  `p=pi^2+b*pi-c` gives residuals forcing `b^2+4c=0`; after localizing at the
   168	  sourced `[1,1]` condition `b^2+4c != 0`, Singular again returns dimension
   169	  `-1`, basis size `1`, and `reduce(1)=0`.
   170	* Fixing the two major weight-42 equality directions is not needed for death.
   171	  Retaining them enlarges the `h3` chart from 7 to 9 coordinates and still
   172	  dies at stage 0.
   173	* The sign is not a free strengthening once the monic top form is fixed:
   174	  `w^2(w-1)^7=-w^2+O(w^3)`.  The charged literal-plus sign control correctly
   175	  rejects the spurious scalar.
   176	* Truncation through local power 8 is a necessary initial-coefficient test for
   177	  `K3=-t^8p+O(t^9)`, not an added equality beyond the source statement.
   178	
   179	Artifacts:
   180	`box/g108gate-20260903/incidence-variants.json`,
   181	`linear-free-cutoff43.out`, and `linear-free-cutoff42.out`.
