    46	
    47	* `DERIVED-SOURCE[FACE-ODE-CLOSED-FORM]`.  Xu's (7.1) at any principal-minor
    48	  split order reduces, for *every* row, to one ODE
    49	
    50	  ```text
    51	  K_g * a * q * p' - b * q' * p = K_g (v_s - u_s) * p^{W+1},
    52	      K_g = n/d_s,  W = (-mu_s-2)/d_s,  deg p = u_s,  deg q = W u_s + 1,
    53	      a = ord T_s(sigma) = W(u_s d - v_s) - 1 + d,  b = ord g(sigma) = K_g(u_s d - v_s).
    54	  ```
    55	
    56	  The right-hand constant is `delta`-independent — `45` at `(99,66)`, `60` at
    57	  `(108,72)` — and `J(f,T_s)` gives the *same* equation, so this is the
    58	  complete leading-order Jacobian content.
    59	* `DERIVED-SOURCE[RESONANCE-SCREEN]`.  At a root of `p` of multiplicity `mm`
    60	  with `ord_q = r`, either `r = W mm + 1` or `K_g a mm = b r` (then also
    61	  `r <= W mm`).  With `sum r_i <= deg q` this reproduces Xu's printed
    62	  `(99,66)` `q`-vectors exactly and settles `D = 108` in four rows.
