   110	is integral as required.
   111	
   112	### 1.2 The five Xu-type orders at `(108,72)`
   113	
   114	`DERIVED-SOURCE`, from Xu §7.3's list `(-mu_i)u_s/d_s`, `((-mu_s-2)u_s/d_s)+1`.
   115	Write `X = u_s delta - v_s = 2 delta - 7`:
   116	
   117	```text
   118	f(sigma)        = p(pi)^8  t^{ 8X} + ...        principal multiplicity 16
   119	g(sigma)        = p(pi)^12 t^{12X} + ...                              24
   120	T_2(sigma)      = p(pi)^7  t^{ 7X} + ...                              14
   121	(T_3)_f(sigma)  = p(pi)^37 t^{37X} + ...                              74
   122	T_3(sigma)      = q(pi)    t^{25X - 1 + delta} + ...   deg q = 25*2+1 = 51
   123	here deg p(pi) = u_3 = 2.
   124	```
   125	
   126	The `(T_3)_f` exponent is Xu's own printed `(-mu_s+n-2)/d_s = 37` (Cor. 7.5),
   127	equal to `W + K_g = 25 + 12`, which is what (7.1)'s order bookkeeping forces.
   128	All five orders are checked in the driver against the **independent** count
   129	`ord X(sigma) = -(#major roots of X) + (#principal roots)*delta` for every
   130	`delta` in `{7/6, ..., 29/6}`, at both rows.  Prop. 6.1's order identity is the
   131	`g` row, `ord g(sigma) = (n/d_s)(u_s delta - v_s) = 12(2 delta - 7)`, so
   132	
   133	```text
   134	ord g(sigma) < 0   <=>   delta < v_s/u_s = 7/2  =  the detector window ceiling.
   135	```
   136	
   137	## 2. Classification of the split orders
   138	
   139	`DERIVED-SOURCE`.  `N5` (`PROVED`, charged `n5-denominator`) gives
   140	`den(delta) <= u_s = 2`; Xu Prop. 7.3 gives `delta > 1`; the ceiling gives
   141	`delta < 7/2`.  Candidates: exactly `{3/2, 2, 5/2, 3}`.  Since `deg p = 2`, the
   142	only partitions are `[2]` (a linear power — Moh's unsplit branch-A analogue,
   143	outside this classification) and `[1,1]` (two simple roots).
   144	
   145	**Route A, printed: Xu Cor. 7.5.**  `u_s = 2 > 1`, and a `[1,1]` split *is* a
   146	split to `u_s` different roots, so every `delta < (v_s+1)/(u_s+1) = 8/3` is
   147	excluded: `3/2, 2, 5/2` die, `3` is untouched.  At `(99,66)` the same corollary
   148	reached only `[1,1,1]` (threshold `9/4`); at `u_s = 2` it is far stronger.
   149	
   150	**Route B, derived: the face-ODE budget.**  `p'`, `q'` are `d/dpi`, not labels.
   151	From `J(g,T_3) = -(T_3)_f J(f,g)` in the `(t,pi)` chart
   152	(`dx ^ dy = -t^{delta-2} dt ^ dpi`), Xu's (7.1) becomes the ODE of §Verdict with
   153	`c = K_g(v_s-u_s) = 60`, `W+1 = 26`.  Screening with
   154	`rho = K_g a/b = (51 delta - 176)/(2 delta - 7)`:
   155	
   156	| `delta` | `a = ord T_3` | `b = ord g` | `rho` | `[1,1]` vectors with `sum r_i <= 51` | verdict |
   157	|---|---:|---:|---:|---|---|
   158	| `3/2` | `-199/2` | `-48` | `199/8` | non-resonant only: `(26,26)`, `52 > 51` | **EXCLUDED** |
   159	| `2`   | `-74`    | `-36` | `74/3`  | non-resonant only: `(26,26)`, `52 > 51` | **EXCLUDED** |
   160	| `5/2` | `-97/2`  | `-24` | `97/4`  | non-resonant only: `(26,26)`, `52 > 51` | **EXCLUDED** |
   161	| `3`   | `-23`    | `-12` | `23`    | `(26,23)` and `(23,23)` | **ALIVE** |
   162	
   163	A `[1,1]` split needs `rho` integral, since `mm = 1` forces `r = rho`; only
   164	`delta = 3` has it.  `FALLACY-v2 / floor-attainment`: "alive" is a screen
   165	survivor, never `FULL_ACTUAL_EXIT`.
   166	
   167	**Galois.**  `den(3) = 1`, so `mu_e` is trivial and imposes nothing; conversely
   168	the translation `pi -> pi + tau` *is* a gauge at integral `delta` (it adds
   169	`tau t^3`, an integral-exponent term, to the common jet).  At half-integral
   170	`delta` neither holds — that asymmetry is what forced `p = pi(pi^2-c)` at
   171	`(99,66)`'s `5/2` and `p = pi^2(pi+3a)` at its `2`.
   172	
   173	### 2.1 The surviving face in closed form, and its rigidity
   174	
   175	`DERIVED-SOURCE`, residual identically zero in SymPy.  At `delta = 3` the ODE
   176	is `p q' - 23 q p' = 5 p^26`; substituting `q = p^23 u` collapses it to
   177	
   178	```text
   179	p^24 * u' = 5 p^26      i.e.      u' = 5 p^2,   deg u = 51 - 46 = 5.
   180	```
   181	
   182	With the translation gauge (`p` monic quadratic, linear term removed) and the
   183	scaling gauge `pi -> lam*pi` (which sends `c -> c/lam^2`, normalising `c = 1`):
   184	
   185	```text
   186	p(pi) = pi^2 - c,  c != 0        (c = 1 after gauge)
   187	u(pi) = pi^5 - (10c/3) pi^3 + 5c^2 pi + e_0,      q = p^23 * u.
   188	```
   189	
   190	**The `delta = 3` face is a 1-parameter family mod gauge**, the parameter being
   191	the integration constant `e_0` — the rigidity class of `(99,66)`'s `5/2` face,
   192	looser than branch B's point.  The ODE does not see `p`'s linear term at all
   193	(checked with `p = pi^2 + b_1 pi + c`), which is why the translation gauge is
   194	the right quotient.
   195	
   196	Internal consistency: `u(±sqrt c) = ±(8/3)c^{5/2} + e_0`, so `u` vanishes at
   197	one root of `p` (giving `r = 23+3 = 26`) for one special `e_0` each, and at both
   198	only if `c = 0` — precisely the budget statement that `(26,26)` is forbidden
   199	while `(26,23)` and `(23,23)` are allowed.
   200	
   201	### 2.2 The split tree is completely determined
   202	
   203	`DERIVED-SOURCE`.  Continuing one packet,
   204	`ord g(sigma') = -84 + (24-g_k)3 + g_k delta'`, final at `0`.  With `g_k = 12`:
   205	
   206	```text
   207	24 principal g-roots  ->  12 + 12,     each 12 g / 8 f,  final at delta' = 4.
   208	Im = 1 + 2*(4-1) = 7.          IM = (n/(n+m)) * 56 * (1 - 3/8) = 21.
   209	sharpened principal floor V_s/u_s = 7/2:   4 >= 7/2 for both packets.
   210	principal places: 24, all e = 1 (delta = 3 is integral, unramified).
   211	```
   212	
   213	No second split is possible: each root of `p` is simple, so each child packet
   214	has `deg p_child = 1`.  (At `(99,66)` branch B the double packet needed Xu
   215	§8(iii)'s `gcd(12,18,10,25) = 1`; here it is automatic.)  Cor. 5.3 passes,
   216	`21 >= 7`: a non-kill, as at `(99,66)`.  The Theorem 3.4 / (4.3) bookkeeping is
   217	again tree-blind — the difference is the constant `m(v_s-u_s)/d_s = 40` for
   218	every `k` and `delta` (`30` at `(99,66)`) — so
   219	`SATURATED-EMPTY[THM-34-EQUALITY-SEPARATION]` carries over, and is moot with
   220	one branch.
