    13	                                                   intersection numbers I(fξ , g) and I(fξ , fy ) respectively, here ξ is a generic element of the base field
    14	                                                   and fξ = f − ξ and discuss usage of them in some special cases. Second, we discuss all possibilities
    15	                                                   of the splits of principal minor roots for the case of degree (99, 66) with help of Abhyankar-Moh
