   266	## 2. The gauges
   267	
   268	Four normalisations. Three are group actions; the fourth (sec 2.4) is not.
   269	
   270	### 2.1 The two lines, the top forms, and `J_0 = 1`
   271	
   272	**Necessity of the shape.** Moh p.194 l.-12 gives
   273	`in g = [(y-ax)^{v_s}(y-bx)^{u_s}]^{n/d_s}` with `a != b`; and, same page,
   274	"Proposition 6.1 implies that the highest homogeneous forms in `x` and `y` of
   275	`T_1^psi,...,T_s^psi` are determined up to constant multiples", of which
   276	`T_1 = f` is the degree-66 member. With `(v_s,u_s,d_s,n,m) = (8,3,11,99,66)`:
   277	`in g = [(y-ax)^8(y-bx)^3]^9`, `in f = c[(y-ax)^8(y-bx)^3]^6`.
   278	
   279	**Group.** `Gamma` = pairs `(A,(lambda,mu))`, `A in GL_2(k)` on `(x,y)`,
   280	`lambda,mu in k*`, `(F,G) -> (lambda(F o A), mu(G o A))`, with source translations
   281	`(x,y) -> (x+c_1, y+c_2)` and target translations `(F,G) -> (F+e_1, G+e_2)`. Each
   282	element preserves Keller (`J_0 -> lambda mu det(A) J_0`), degrees, and the
   283	characteristic data.
   284	
   285	**Orbit representative.** (i) Some `A` sends the independent forms `y-ax`, `y-bx`
   286	to `y-x`, `y`, uniquely up to the 2-torus scaling them separately; then
   287	`in(F o A) = c''P^9`, `in(G o A) = c'P^6`, `P = y^3(y-x)^8`. (ii) `lambda = 1/c''`,
   288	`mu = 1/c'` makes both monic with `deg = deg_y`. (iii) The residual freedom
   289	`F -> s'^{-99}F(sx,s'y)`, `G -> s'^{-66}G(sx,s'y)` fixes `y = 0`, sends `y = x` to
   290	`y = (s/s')x`, and multiplies `J_0` by `s s'^{-164}`; keeping the major line at
   291	`y = x` forces `s = s'`, and the remaining one-parameter group scales `J_0` by
   292	`s^{-163}`, so algebraically closed `k` supplies `s` with `s^{163} = J_0`. Hence
   293	
   294	```text
   295	in F = P^9,  in G = P^6,  P = y^3(y-x)^8,  J(F,G) = 1
   296	```
   297	
   298	is a legitimate representative: **the torus parameter `a = 1` in
   299	`P_a = y^3(y-ax)^8` and the normalisation `J_0 = 1` are the same single gauge.**
   300	`J_0 != 0` is not a gauge but the Keller hypothesis; only `J_0 = 1` is imposed.
   301	
   302	The multiplicities follow: `in F = y^{27}(y-x)^{72}`, `in G = y^{18}(y-x)^{48}`,
   303	matching Moh **Prop 6.2** (p.195): `deg_y g-hat = v_s n/d_s = 72`,
   304	`deg_z g-hat = u_s n/d_s = 27`, and `48/18` for `f`.
