   312	### 2.4 The two constant centres -- the one normalisation that is not free
   313	
   314	New finding; source of `GAP[TWO-CENTRE-NORMALISATION]`. The chart uses
   315	simultaneously
   316	
   317	```text
   318	major D_2 general point : w = 1 + pi t^{4/3}          (i.e.  w_0 = 0)
   319	minor general point     : w = a_0 t + u t^2 + z t^3   with a_0 = 0.
   320	```
   321	
   322	Both come from Moh Definition 5.1(4), `sigma_i = sum_j w_j t^j + pi t^{delta_i}`:
   323	for `D_2` the centre is `t^{-1} + w_0` (the exponents `< delta_2 = 1/3` are `-1`
   324	and `0`); for the minor disc Moh p.209 writes `a_{-1}t^{-1} + a_0 + a_1 t`, and
   325	the minor line at `y = 0` forces `a_{-1} = 0` (linear gauge) while `a_1 = u` stays
   326	free. Two constants remain.
   327	
   328	**The gauge is one-dimensional.** The only element of `Gamma` moving them is
   329	`y -> y - b`, under which `w_0 -> w_0 - b`, `a_0 -> a_0 - b`; so `w_0 - a_0` is a
   330	gauge invariant. **What it normalises:** the 11 roots of `h3` are 8 major
   331	(`= x + w_0 + O(x^{-1/3})`) and 3 minor (`= a_0 + O(x^{-1})`), summing to
   332	`-[y^{10}]h3 = 8x - h_{10}` with `h_{10} := [y^{10}]H` a constant
   333	(`deg H <= 10`), so comparing constant terms
   334	
   335	```text
   336	8 w_0 + 3 a_0 = - h_{10},      h_{10} -> h_{10} - 11 b
   337	```
   338	
   339	(the same computation with `F` gives `9(8w_0+3a_0)`, with `G` gives
   340	`6(8w_0+3a_0)`: no new information). Hence in the gauge `h_{10} = 0` the
   341	conditions `w_0 = 0` and `a_0 = 0` are equivalent to each other, and each is
   342	**one scalar condition beyond the gauge**.
