   374	## 3. The outer `D_2` support preblock and the `D_1` boundary bands
   375	
   376	### 3.1 Statement and source
   377	
   378	The eight inequalities of sec 1.3 are the whole content: Moh Theorem 1.2 (p.149)
   379	supplies them, Moh Proposition 6.2 (p.195) the multiplicities, Definition 5.1(3)
   380	(p.179) the radii. **No equality face is imposed on the outer blocks:**
   381	Theorem 1.2 is a `>=` statement, so only strictly-below slots become rows.
   382	
   383	### 3.2 The weight cut, derived
   384	
   385	Homogenise `Q in S(D,33)` by
   386	`K_Q(t,w) = t^D Q(t^{-1}, w/t) = sum Qc_{r,q} t^r (w-1)^q`, `r >= 0`, `q < 33`,
   387	`r+q <= D` -- an invertible change of basis (triangular from `x^i y^j`, with
   388	`r = D - i - j`). Then `Q(t^{-1},sigma) = t^{-D}K_Q(t,w)`.
   389	
   390	**`D_2`.** With `w = 1 + pi t^{4/3}`, `t = s^3`: `t^r(w-1)^q = pi^q s^{3r+4q}`, so
   391	`W(r,q) = 3r+4q` is the exact `s`-weight. Distinct slots of equal weight carry
   392	distinct powers of `pi`, so **no cancellation between slots is possible** and
   393	`ord_s K_Q = min{W : Qc != 0}`. The bound `ord_t Q >= B` therefore reads
   394	`W(r,q) >= 3(D+B)` on every occupied slot, i.e. `Qc_{r,q} = 0` whenever
   395	`3r+4q < 3(D+B)`: a **unit** row per slot.
   396	
   397	| block | `D` | `B` | `3(D+B)` | ambient | deleted | remaining | min `r` left |
   398	|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
   399	| `A2` | 65 | `-2` | 189 | 1650 | 1386 | 264 | 21 |
   400	| `A3` | 98 | `-3` | 285 | 2739 | 2442 | 297 | 53 |
   401	| `B1` | 32 | `-1` | 93 | 561 | 384 | 177 | 0 |
   402	| `B2` | 65 | `-2` | 189 | 1650 | 1386 | 264 | 21 |
   403	| total | | | | **6600** | **5598** | **1002** | |
   404	
   405	(recomputed here from the thresholds alone). Two consequences used later: the whole degree-`D` face of `A2, A3, B2` is deleted
   406	(`A2` has `4q <= 128 < 189` at `r = 0`) while `B1` survives at `r = 0` for
   407	`q >= 24`; and **through `t`-power 21 the identities `KF = K2^3` and
   408	`KG = K2^2 + tK_{B1}K2` are exact**, since `A2, B2` first survive at `r = 21` and
   409	`A3` at `r = 53`.
   410	
   411	**`D_1`.** With `t = e^9`, `w = 1 + e^{12} + Pi e^{13}`, a remaining slot
   412	contributes `Qc_{r,q}e^{9r+12q}(1+Pi e)^q`, so the coefficient of `Pi^j e^E` is
   413	`sum_{9r+12q+j = E} binom(q,j) Qc_{r,q}`, and `ord_t Q >= B_1` says all rows with
   414	`E < 9(D+B_1)` vanish. Thresholds `583, 879, 287, 583`. Unlike `D_2` these are
   415	**not** unit rows: several `(r,q)` share one `(E,j)`.
   416	
   417	### 3.3 The exact `D_1` rank, recomputed
   418	
   419	`D_2` has already forced `9r+12q >= 3 x (D_2 threshold)`, so the `D_1` rows live
   420	in a finite window:
   421	
   422	| block | `e`-window | raw `(E,j)` rows | exact `Q`-rank |
   423	|---|---|---:|---:|
   424	| `A2` | `[567,582]` | 51 | 44 |
   425	| `A3` | `[855,878]` | 108 | 73 |
   426	| `B1` | `[279,286]` | 15 | 15 |
   427	| `B2` | `[567,582]` | 51 | 44 |
   428	| total | | **225** | **176** |
   429	
   430	so `1002 - 176 = 826` outer coordinates survive. Recomputed here by exact
   431	Gaussian elimination on the integer binomial matrix; the 49 dependent rows reduce
   432	identically to zero (slot dependencies, not a cokernel obstruction). The same
   433	driver reproduces the *major* `h2` `D_1` band: 7 rows at `e`-powers
   434	`291:1, 292:1, 293:1, 294:2, 295:2`, rank 7. Every pivot is a nonzero rational and
   435	`rho, c, u, v` do not occur, so these rows are branch-independent and imposed
   436	identically in both branches (they constrain the *first* point).
