   438	### 3.4 Scale-independence of the `D_1` block
   439	
   440	With centre offset `alpha e^{12}`, `alpha != 0`, one has
   441	`t^r(w-1)^q = alpha^q e^{9r+12q}(1 + (Pi/alpha)e)^q`, so the `(E,j),(r,q)` entry
   442	becomes `binom(q,j)alpha^{q-j}`. Since `j` depends only on the row and `q` only
   443	on the column,
   444	
   445	```text
   446	M(alpha) = diag(alpha^{-j}) . M(1) . diag(alpha^{q}),
   447	```
   448	
   449	both diagonal factors invertible. Hence the raw counts and the exact ranks
   450	`44/73/15/44` (and 7 for `h2`) are **independent of `alpha != 0`**, and the row
   451	space of `M(alpha)` is the image of that of `M(1)` under
   452	`Qc_{r,q} -> alpha^q Qc_{r,q}`. Not established: that this substitution is a
   453	symmetry of the other row families simultaneously. See `N4`.
