   710	(B) split at delta = 2   with p = pi^2(pi+3a), a != 0   ([2,1]);
   711	(C) split at delta = 5/2 with p = pi(pi^2-c),  c != 0   ([1,1,1]).
   712	```
   713	
   714	*Proof.* Write `delta` for the split order, `p` for the leading polynomial,
   715	`deg p = u_s = 3`; Xu Prop 7.3 (whose proof shows `p` is a linear power at order
   716	1) gives `delta > 1`.
